% Benchmark program: non-tail user-function recursion, exercised by
% `bench/scheme/bench/harness.sls` through the `sum` case.
%
% `sum(N)` walks N down through one equation chain per level, so the case
% measures user-function dispatch, equation pattern matching and the
% prelude arithmetic/comparison helpers on the hottest possible path.
% It is the shape whose generated code used to capture a `call/cc`
% continuation on every level (and once more for each prelude helper
% it called), which is the Scheme backend's dominant recursion cost.
%
% The result is N*(N+1)/2: 2001000 at N = 2000, which is the value the
% harness checks.
:- module(bench_sum, [go/2]).

:- chr_constraint go/2.

:- function sum(int) -> int.

sum(0) -> 0.
sum(N) | N > 0 -> N + sum(N - 1).

go(N, R) <=> R is sum(N).
